d Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 10:07PM MDT until October 23 at 11:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Saguache County in central Colorado...\nMineral County in south central Colorado...\nRio Grande County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 AM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Several structures are flooded and sand bagging\noperations are continuing. Evacuations are occuring from Wolf Creek\nRanch to Fun Valley. Some roads remain closed due to flooding\nincluding highway 160 and FR380.  The Park Creek bridge has been\nwashed away with considerable debris in the water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1002 PM MDT, emergency management reported heavy rain in the\nwarned area. Flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\nBetween 1 and 3.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the\nwarned area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nThe Rio Grande River and its tributaries including the South Fork\narea and along highway 160 to Wolf Creek Pass.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T11:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.03011cf1c8199da5de650405af1eee2a145ac204.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.03011cf1c8199da5de650405af1eee2a145ac204.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 9:43PM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Ample sub-tro